    "what": "Strength of the pre-execution gate, strongest first: M1 and K0 deny every package command until it carries a review marker the agent itself writes; L1 denies the first attempt and lets the identical command through within 30 minutes; K1 blocks only commands without an exact version; M and L0 allow and remind afterwards. None verifies that the checks were done (the markers and the retry are self-attested). PROBE-HOOK-01 (HOOK_PROBE_RESULTS.json, direct script runs, same command twice): `dotnet add <Api> package Serilog.AspNetCore --version 8.0.3` -> M allow/allow, L0 allow/allow, K1 allow/allow, L1 deny/allow (identical retry within 30 minutes passes, pre-shell-command.mjs:7-8), M1 deny/deny and K0 deny/deny until the command carries the self-attested marker `# add-dependency: checked` (M1 dependency-commands.js:15/:528) or `# add-dependency: reviewed` (K0 hook.cjs:18/:294); without --version K1 also blocks (exit 2, classify-command.cjs:224 'without an exact version'). The same pattern holds for `npm install left-pad@1.3.0` (matches v3 SAME_TASK_MATRIX 'pinned install, first attempt'). M and L0 rely on PostToolUse reminders to confirm the add-dependency steps (M dependency-guard.mjs:278, L0 claude-hook.mjs:555-557).",
    "counterexample": "Same task: 'add Serilog logging'. The agent runs `dotnet add src/Api package Serilog.AspNetCore --version 8.0.3` without having checked deprecation, vulnerabilities or license. M1 and K0 refuse it until the agent re-runs with the marker; L1 refuses once; K1, M and L0 execute it immediately, M and L0 then remind. Live-host handling of deny NOT_RUN.",
